  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale\n\n1.1 Central idea\nThe requested objective\n\n  C\u2085(h) = max_k [np.correlate(h, 1-h, \"full\")] * dx\n\nis finite-dimensional but nonsmooth and nonconvex. The plan optimizes the same rebuilt discrete representation of the parent problem wherever feasible. The main local engine optimizes a log-sum-exp smoothed approximation to the maximum, but no candidate is accepted on smooth value alone: every candidate is repaired to strict feasibility and scored with the original exact maximum using the prescribed np.correlate formula. A fallback is the best feasible current construction (the supplied parent, if valid), so the returned lower C5 is never worse than the validated parent.\n\nThe proposed search uses a sequence of resolutions anchored around the supplied 45-point parent. At each resolution it evolves a small population of feasible vectors using local smooth maximum optimization, perturbations around the best members, structured seed generators, and multi-lambda smoothing. A small amount of extra refinement is applied to the best population member before returning. The method is intentionally local/nonconvex and has no global-optimality guarantee; improvements are claimed only through exact recomputation.\n\n1.2 Why this can improve the parent\nSmoothing each lag constraint by log-sum-exp converts the nonsmooth expression into differentiable functions on the same feasible set and gives a usable gradient that mostly follows the currently most-violating lag constraints. Taking lambda successively larger moves the surrogate toward the exact max. Because every final run is evaluated with the original max rather than the smoother, an apparent local descent of the smoother is allowed to be corrected only if exact value validates. Feasibility repair with a joint scaling/projection mechanism keeps steps inside the same feasible set, preserving the original constraint.\n\nThe exact evaluation cost is an O(n^2) local operation with low memory use for n in the 45\u201391 range. Smoothing makes objective iterations near the parent inefficient by using coarse multi-start loops. The parent reward relaxation plus smoothing global variance causal structures is claimed here and robust implements some target-site adjustments.\n\nHowever, absent global certify exact result. An adaptive scheduled limit, streak limits, if necessary persist long otherwise through run-time - that's generation rather-down argument concentrates remaining quota to the improved performers retains old seeds while additionally custom prioritizes flows.",
